record audit.observation.fact-layer-surface-gap/7 : observation {
    title "M1 inventory complete; xref sections and signature crypto remain"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Updated after the M1 completion pass. Three former pending sections landed end to end and are gone from the report: linearization (pdf-read detects a valid /Linearized first object; pdf-forensics carries LinearizationFacts); per-annotation identity (PageAnnotation now keeps source ObjectId, /Contents, /NM, /M, /CreationDate, /T, /Subj and /IT, surfaced as AnnotationIdentityFacts in page order alongside the existing per-subtype counts); and marked-content edit markers (pdf-content exposes MarkedContentSpan with tag name and bbox; pdf-forensics reports per-page /TouchUp_* spans with tag, content-stream open/close offsets and text bbox). The fixture gap is closed too: pdf-test-support builds an RC4 document under a non-empty user password the standard handler accepts, and encrypted_modes covers the StructureOnly-to-Full upgrade on the same file.

        Two sections remain pending, both outside M1 by the ledger's own account: per-xref-section offsets, types and entry counts (needs the XrefSection type from @audit.decision.revision-model; M2 work) and signature cryptography (structural ByteRange coverage is reported; verification itself is M4).

        The lege-pdf-audit binary now ships `inspect` with terminal and JSON output, the ten-fixture M1 suite is green, and a PDF-Verse-style export reports all pages raster-only with zero visible text, zero embedded fonts, and disposition INCONCLUSIVE. M1's four acceptance checks are satisfied with evidence; @audit.work.edit-provenance-facts and the M1 plan of record are complete.

        Still true from /6: the XMP parser is a targeted local-name scanner, not a general XML parser, and accepts a theoretical cross-namespace local-name collision in exchange for working with non-standard prefixes.
        """
    observed_at git:883393dc473bf5288501b4e619688a4bfb68bcf9
    method manual
    watches [ "crates/pdf-forensics/src/intake.rs", "crates/pdf-forensics/src/document.rs" ]
    supersedes [ @audit.observation.fact-layer-surface-gap/6 ]
}

